nce of NOT LESS than two credible witnesses is necessary.&lt;br /&gt; (iv)  See Section 160(4) and (5) for details re. election penalties which may apply for this offence.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code>EWAY</code><description>EITHER WAY</description></modeoftrial><timelimitforprosecutions>Complex</timelimitforprosecutions><penalty>SUMMARY: Six months imprisonment and / or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.&lt;br /&gt;INDICTMENT: Two years imprisonment and / or a fine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Time limit for prosecutions:&lt;br /&gt;Complex&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;On the 12th March 2015 the limit on fines imposed by a Magistrates’ court was removed – as such, the potential fine on summary conviction in relation to an offence committed after this date is unlimited.</penalty><geographicregion><code>UK</code><description>United Kingdom</description></geographicregion></other><codes><cjsoffencecode>RP83002</cjsoffencecode><recordableonpncindicator><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></recordableonpncindicator><pncacpooffencecode>7.8.10.2</pncacpooffencecode><notifiabletoho><code>Y</code><description>Yes</description></notifiabletoho><hoclassification>099/06</hoclassification><mopireviewgroup><code>C</code><description>Group 3</description></mopireviewgroup><mopinoteslink>D19586</mopinoteslink><disqualificationclass><code>N</code><description>discretionary disqualification not endorsable</description></disqualificationclass><seatbeltoffence><code>N</code><description>No</description></seatbeltoffence><fptissuedbypolice>0</fptissuedbypolice><fptgraduated>0</fptgraduated><fptgraduatedhigh>0</fptgraduatedhigh><pndissuedbypolice>0</pndissuedbypolice><pndissuedbylocalauthorities>0</p